. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2
. 
.         
.         * We estimate a linear probability model with our constructed indicat
> or of left political preferences (left) as the dependent variable on the numb
> er of daughters (ndaughters)
.         * as the treatment variable and further control variables (number of 
> children, marital status, sex, age, age squared, household income, household 
> size education
.         * labor force status and the survey year). To account for individual 
> heterogeneity, we include individual fixed effects.
.         * A positive coefficient on the number of daughters (with a p-value s
> maller than 0.1) empirically supports H2.
.         
.         xtset pid syear

Panel variable: pid (unbalanced)
 Time variable: syear, 2000 to 2020, but with gaps
         Delta: 1 unit

.         xtreg left ndaughters i.nchildren i.pgfamstd i.sex age age_sq hghinc 
> hhsize i.pgisced97 i.pglfs i.syear, fe
